WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.840
Do you have any memories of any specific hurricane where you witnessed things happen during the hurricane?

2
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:08.440
Yes.

3
00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:13.200
We evacuated for Betsy and we went to Westwego.

4
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.580
I was a little boy, and Roger [Camardelle],

5
00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:24.540
all the Camardelles got together at my grandmother's house in Avenue A. And I'll never forget [meteorologist] Nash Roberts with his little black crayon circling,

6
00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:27.080
it was a black and white television, "It's not going to hit."

7
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.700
About ten o'clock that night, "It's not going to be bad."

8
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.700
All of a sudden my grandmother's roof come off in Westwego.

9
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.660
And I remember we all ran.

10
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:43.940
Sheets of tin were flying on Avenue A. I remember running to my other aunt's house which was next door, and we're all piling up.

11
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.040
Believe it or not, my Uncle Roger, his wife, Aunt Lois,

12
00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:52.320
they forgot their baby in the little . . . one of the babies because he was underneath the table.

13
00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.440
And that's the young man that y'all rode in the boat with today with was Noel.

14
00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:55.800
Really.

15
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.040
Noel was in that baby crib.

16
00:00:59.040 --> 00:00:59.960
And she goes, "Oh!"

17
00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.560
She had five or six of them and she goes, "We forgot Noel!"

18
00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:04.860
So they went back, run in the house.

19
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.840
It was still raining, but he was underneath the table and they grabbed the baby.

20
00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.240
And I tease Noel, I said, "Sometimes I bet you we should've left you over there!" [Camardelle and Robicheaux laugh] But it was crazy,

21
00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.480
but it's one of the memories—I was a young boy, and I remember that we all had to run for Betsy.
